		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Incorrect radio type selected during RT-3S DM-1701 update]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5085&amp;p=36912#p36912"><![CDATA[
Dear all,<br>today I updated both of my radios, a DM1701 and an RT3S to latest firmware.<br>When flashing the RT3S, I forgot to change the type in the popup window leaving it on  DM1701, but selecting the correct zip file for the RT3S.<br>The radio flashed the firmware and then restarted only in bootloader mode, green and red flashing continuously.<br>I then realized the mistake, corrected it, flashed correctly and now the radio appears to be working fine, transmitting and receiving, both FM and DMR.<br><br>I would like to ask here the programmer "gurus" here if this may corrupted something in the memory and I need to restore some of the backups or if is safe to leave it as is now.<br><br>Thank you!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7229">IU1INZ</a> — Sat Apr 26, 2025 7:30 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
